<h2>Kachikally Crocodile Pool, Bakau, Gambia</h2>
<p>The <strong>Kachikally Crocodile Pool</strong> in Bakau, Gambia, is a sacred site and one of the most unique tourist places in Gambia.
    This cultural landmark is home to over 100 crocodiles, where visitors can experience a rare opportunity to see these ancient reptiles up
    close. Located near major tourist hubs and not far from <strong>Banjul Airport</strong>, it is easily accessible for those exploring the
    <strong>beautiful places in Gambia</strong>.</p>

<h2>Abuko Nature Reserve, Abuko, Gambia</h2>
<p>The <strong>Abuko Nature Reserve</strong> is Gambia’s oldest protected nature reserve and a must-visit on any <strong>Gambia map</strong>
    of natural attractions. Situated in Abuko, this reserve offers a glimpse into Gambia’s rich biodiversity, making it a top choice for
    nature lovers looking for <strong>places in Gambia</strong> that are rich in wildlife. Conveniently located near <strong>Banjul
        International Airport</strong>, it’s an easy stop for visitors arriving at the <strong>Gambia airport</strong>.</p>

<h2>Bijilo Forest Park, Bijilo, Gambia</h2>
<p><strong>Bijilo Forest Park</strong>, also known as Monkey Park, is one of the <strong>beautiful places in Gambia</strong> that should not
    be missed. Located in Bijilo, this coastal park is a haven for wildlife, including various species of monkeys. A visit here is a perfect
    addition to exploring the <strong>best beaches in Gambia</strong>, as it’s just a short drive from popular beach resorts.</p>

<h2>Albert Market, Banjul, Gambia</h2>
<p><strong>Albert Market</strong> in Banjul is one of the most vibrant <strong>places in Gambia</strong>. This bustling market is an
    essential part of the city’s culture, offering everything from fresh produce to handcrafted goods. A visit here provides insight into
    the daily life of Gambians and is a must for anyone exploring <strong>tourist places in Gambia</strong>.</p>

<h2>Tanji Village Museum, Tanji, Gambia</h2>
<p>The <strong>Tanji Village Museum</strong> in Tanji offers a deep dive into the cultural heritage of Gambia. This museum showcases
    traditional Gambian life, making it one of the key <strong>places in Gambia</strong> to visit for those interested in history and
    culture. It’s also conveniently located near some of the <strong>best beaches in Gambia</strong>, allowing visitors to combine a
    cultural tour with a relaxing day by the ocean.</p>

<h2>Sanyang Beach, Sanyang, Gambia</h2>
<p><strong>Sanyang Beach</strong> is widely regarded as one of the <strong>best beaches in Gambia</strong>. Known for its golden sands and
    tranquil atmosphere, it is a top destination for tourists seeking the perfect beach day. Located away from the busier areas, this serene
    beach offers a glimpse of <strong>beautiful places in Gambia</strong> that are still relatively untouched by mass tourism.</p>

<h2>Makasutu Culture Forest, Makasutu, Gambia</h2>
<p>The <strong>Makasutu Culture Forest</strong> in Makasutu is one of the most diverse <strong>places in Gambia</strong> for nature and
    culture. This forest reserve is known for its rich wildlife, traditional villages, and cultural performances, offering a comprehensive
    experience of Gambian life. It’s a must-visit for those looking to explore <strong>beautiful places in Gambia</strong> that combine
    nature with culture.</p>

<h2>National Museum of Gambia, Banjul, Gambia</h2>
<p>The <strong>National Museum of Gambia</strong> in Banjul is one of the most important <strong>tourist places in Gambia</strong> for
